    "letter": "D",
    "heading": "Skąd jesteś? Gdzie mieszkasz?",
    "meaning": {
      "en": "Where are you from? Where do you live?"
    },
    "strands": [
      "G"
    ]
  },
  "tips": [
    {
      "id": "kpk1-l02-d4-t01",
      "before": "kpk1-l02-d4-e01",
      "title": {
        "en": "Verbs in -m and -sz"
      },
      "body": {
        "en": "Many verbs go like *mam* and *mieszkam*: *-m* for \"I\" and *-sz* for \"you\". So *grać* (to play) is *gram*, *grasz*, *gra*; *czytać* (to read) is *czytam*, *czytasz*; and *rozumieć* is *rozumiem*, *rozumiesz*."
      },
      "conjugation": {
        "verb": "grać",
        "meaning": {
          "en": "to play"
        },
        "forms": {
          "ja": "gram",
          "ty": "grasz",
          "on": "gra",
          "my": "gramy",
          "wy": "gracie",
          "oni": "grają"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "kpk1-l02-d4-t02",
      "before": "kpk1-l02-d4-e05",
      "title": {
        "en": "What do you like doing?"
      },
      "body": {
        "en": "*Gram w tenisa* is \"I play tennis\". *Czytam* is \"I read\", *oglądam serial* \"I watch a series\", and *kocham* is \"I love\": *kocham Kraków*. These are hobbies: *to moje hobby*."
      }
    }
  ],
